# go.work.example — copy to `go.work` for local multi-module dev (the four modules resolve against
# each other without re-publishing). `go.work` itself is gitignored on purpose: a committed go.work
# would be visible inside the gate container (the repo is mounted at /src) and the checkables would
# resolve `manifest` via the workspace `use` directive instead of the published `require` — masking
# exactly the property the gate proves. CI's fresh checkout has no go.work, so CI exercises the real
# published-dep path. NOTE: a parent go.work exists at ../go.work; this repo-root go.work shadows it
# (Go selects the nearest go.work walking up from the module dir) — the nesting is intentional.
go 1.26.5

use (
	.
	.dagger
	.dagmar
	manifest
)
